 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Pop it in the frame shell on both sides and see if it' level. If it's too low, you can add a washer. You should feel a smooth resistance that feels about right. If it feels too easy, your seat tube is too deep. Nothing. Just checking that the seat tube is the right depth. Then you can use a washer under the bolt. Then your seat tube is too deep. You can use a washer under the bolt to lower it. Which do you prefer? You might not reach the same low point, but you' still be level. If it feels right, go for it.",
